  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Electrical Contractors and Other Wiring Installation Contractors (NAICS 238210): Federal contract obligations total $652M in FY2026 to date. The market has produced 2,577 awards so far, with an average award size of $253K. Obligations are down 17.6% year over year. Fiscal-year history shows fluctuations: FY21 obligations were $792M, FY22 obligations were $853M, FY23 obligations were $945M, FY24 obligations were $824M, FY25 obligations were $791M, and FY26 obligations are $652M. The current-year totals are partial and represent fiscal year to date activity. This profile is focused on contract obligations, not on procurement forecasts or pipeline signals. Buyers and suppliers should treat FY2026 to date as an incomplete year when comparing to full prior fiscal years.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies buy the most NAICS 238210 services?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $155M, the Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $153M, and the Department of State obligated $126M in FY2026 to date. The Department of Transportation obligated $71.8M and the Department of Homeland Security obligated $45.8M. Remaining top buyers include the Department of Justice with $34.9M and the Department of the Interior with $20.3M. Smaller but notable buyers include the Department of Agriculture with $8.6M, the Department of Health and Human Services with $7.8M, and the General Services Administration with $7.7M."
      },
